    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The helper returns a fetch `Response`, but Google Calendar immediately reads `res?.data.access_token` and `res?.data.expiry_date`. A raw `Response` does not provide token fields on `.data`, so when credential sharing is enabled and the sync endpoint is used, token refresh produces `undefined` token values and the credential update stores the wrong data. Also observed in: packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/refreshOAuthTokens.ts",
